-- title:
--   Twisted hyperbolic cell at σ=1 equals untwisted cell
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $\alpha,\beta$ real numbers, $\Phi_1,\Phi_2$ subsets of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, $\nu_{Z,K}$ a measure and $\Omega_K$ a subset of the idele group $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$, $D$ a Galois descent datum for the trivial extension $K/K$ (a monoid homomorphism $(K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}K)\to\mathrm{Aut}(\mathbb{A}_K)$ compatible with $K\to\mathbb{A}_K$ and with continuous values), $hgen$ a proof that every $\tau\in K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}K$ lies in the cyclic group generated by $1$, $\xi$ a homomorphism from the full subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, and $\varphi:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathbb{C}$. Then for every real $R$ the following two integrals over the canonical truncation domain attached to $(\alpha,\beta)$, against the Haar measure of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ for its Borel structure, coincide. Both have inner integral $\int_{\Omega_K}\xi(z)\,(A(z,x)-B(z,x))\,d\nu_{Z,K}$. On the left, $A$ is the unordered sum of $\varphi(x^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(z\cdot x))$ over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ whose $1$-twisted conjugacy class has twisted-norm class (the class map attached to $hgen$) equal to the conjugacy class of some $\gamma$ of hyperbolic type, i.e. with characteristic polynomial $(X-a)(X-b)$, $a\neq b$; here $\delta$ and $z$ are pushed into the adeles by $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ and by the central scalar embedding, and $\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}$ is the automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ induced by $D$ at the identity automorphism. On the right, $A$ is the hyperbolic part of the adelic kernel, $\sum_{\gamma\text{ hyperbolic}}\varphi(x^{-1}\gamma\,(z\cdot x))$. In both, $B$ is the indicator of the set where the adelic height exceeds $e^R$, evaluated at $z\cdot x$, times the constant term along the unipotent matrices $\binom{1\ t}{0\ 1}$ of the corresponding truncation function: on the left the sum of $\varphi(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(y))$ over upper-triangular $\delta$ with $N_{K/K}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11})\neq 1$, on the right the sum of $\varphi(x^{-1}\gamma\,y)$ over upper-triangular $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}\neq 1$. The two constant terms are taken against the measure component of the production pins built from $(\Phi_1,$ the levels $\mathrm{levelOne}\sqcap\mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, the Hecke generators, the adelic box$)$ and from $(\Phi_2,$ the levels $\mathrm{principalLevel}\sqcap\mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, the Hecke generators, the adelic box$)$ respectively; by definition this component is in both cases the additive adelic Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box, so neither $\Phi_1,\Phi_2$ nor the level families enter it.
--
--   This is the comparison, for the degenerate "cyclic extension" $K/K$ with generator the identity automorphism, between the $\sigma$-twisted hyperbolic term of the truncated $\mathrm{GL}_2$ trace formula and the ordinary hyperbolic term: at $\sigma=1$ the twisted norm map is trivial and the $\sigma$-twisted hyperbolic cell reduces to the set of elements of hyperbolic type, while the twisted adelic action is the identity. It is used by the results that extract the affine behaviour of the hyperbolic term and its limit along the truncation parameter, in the analysis of the winding datum and of class integrals.
